WEBVTT

00:01.100 --> 00:04.520
"It seems today that all you see

00:04.646 --> 00:08.065
"Is violence in movies and sex on TV

00:08.190 --> 00:11.822
"But where are those
good old-fashioned values

00:11.946 --> 00:14.656
"On which we used to rely?

00:14.739 --> 00:17.993
"Lucky there's a family guy

00:18.076 --> 00:23.204
"Lucky there's a man who positively
can do all the things that make us

00:23.204 --> 00:24.667
"Laugh and cry

00:24.752 --> 00:30.173
"He's a family guy

00:34.052 --> 00:38.307
Peter, this is ridiculous.
I know you're upset about losing your job,

00:38.430 --> 00:40.391
but you've sat there for two weeks.

00:40.517 --> 00:44.355
- I have not, Lois.
- He's right. It's actually been more like...

00:44.481 --> 00:48.107
- Yeah. 13 days.
- You have to do something other than eat.

00:48.233 --> 00:52.405
All right, all right. Brian, let's go for a walk.

01:01.664 --> 01:04.708
Meg, sweetheart, what's wrong?

01:04.793 --> 01:09.380
My life. That's what's wrong.
I was totally humiliated at school today.

01:09.505 --> 01:12.426
We're gonna do an informal survey here, kids.

01:12.426 --> 01:18.056
Would those who are going away for spring
break please move to the left of the room?

01:18.766 --> 01:24.938
Oigan, quienes van a spring break,
pasen a la izquierda, por favor.

01:24.938 --> 01:28.484
- Meg, what do those kids know?
- They know how to have a good time.

01:28.566 --> 01:33.488
So do we. I'll tell you what. How about you
and I have our own little spring break?

01:33.571 --> 01:36.410
We'll go to that fancy new spa
that just opened up.

01:36.493 --> 01:40.579
Massages and facials.
It'll be great. What do you say?

01:40.579 --> 01:44.960
I guess it couldn't be worse than last year
when we all went to Sea World.

01:49.340 --> 01:51.719
And how long has this been going on?!

01:54.970 --> 01:57.556
Lois is right. I've been out of work too long.

01:57.681 --> 02:00.476
I think you should find
something you enjoy doing.

02:00.600 --> 02:03.938
- Take those guys out there, for example.
- Where?

02:06.231 --> 02:10.069
Oh, yeah. Now, that's a job.
Fresh sea air, working outside.

02:10.195 --> 02:12.697
That's how a real New England man
makes a living.

02:12.779 --> 02:16.035
- That's something to think about.
- What's that, Daddy?

02:16.035 --> 02:19.370
That's Mercury, Jake,
the planet closest to the sun.

02:19.454 --> 02:22.584
What it's doing by the wharf,
we should ask a scientist...

02:22.710 --> 02:24.585
I'm a guy, you jackass!

02:25.918 --> 02:28.212
Ah, yeah, that feels good.

02:28.339 --> 02:31.133
Chris, don't forget to mist under his chins.

02:31.258 --> 02:34.888
Oh, boy, Lois. It's a real mess down there.

02:35.013 --> 02:38.016
I'm afraid I'm won't be able
to do this in the time I quoted.

02:38.141 --> 02:41.979
Chris, shut the hose off for a second.
I have an announcement.

02:42.104 --> 02:45.232
I am gonna drop this weight
and rejoin the workforce.

02:45.316 --> 02:48.362
I have decided to become
a professional fisherman.

02:48.362 --> 02:49.904
What? Why a fisherman?

02:50.029 --> 02:53.448
It makes sense. You know
how much time I've spent on the ocean.

02:53.573 --> 02:58.246
Wilson! What are we gonna do now?!

02:58.372 --> 03:03.793
- Wilson! Wilson!
- My name is Voit, dumb-ass.

03:04.293 --> 03:07.421
Hello, Doreen?
I'm still over at the Griffin job.

03:07.546 --> 03:11.176
Tell Walter I won't be able
to make it to the construction site.

03:11.300 --> 03:15.972
So... I don't know. Have him send
Frank or Glen or Harelip Steve.

03:16.098 --> 03:18.599
I know, it creeps me out, too.

03:20.476 --> 03:22.562
So you think I can find a boat here?

03:22.647 --> 03:25.775
You wouldn't believe what we
confiscate from these crooks.

03:25.900 --> 03:30.571
We open today's bidding with this pair
of panties confiscated from a prostitute.

03:30.697 --> 03:33.072
- 50 bucks!
- She had nine STD's.

03:33.825 --> 03:37.371
- 45 bucks.
- And when we caught her, she wet herself.

03:37.453 --> 03:42.377
- 50 bucks.
- Will you sell anything that's not gross?

03:42.459 --> 03:47.172
Please direct your attention to this photo
of a beautiful 40-foot fishing boat.

03:47.172 --> 03:49.674
- Oh, man, that's perfect!
- $12,000.

03:49.759 --> 03:52.802
- $13,000.
- $25,000.

03:52.885 --> 03:55.724
- Sold for $25,000.
- Yes!

03:55.724 --> 03:57.890
- Aw, crap!
- Thanks.

03:58.017 --> 04:01.855
And now the actual boat itself.
Do I have an opening bid for the boat?

04:01.980 --> 04:04.899
- $50,000!
- Sold for $50,000.

04:04.982 --> 04:07.696
Good for you, Peter.

04:10.322 --> 04:13.868
Congratulations.
You've bought yourself a cursed boat.

04:13.952 --> 04:16.870
- Cursed?
- The last captain of that vessel lost his life.

04:16.996 --> 04:20.000
And it weren't no accident!
His name was Salty.

04:20.124 --> 04:23.544
And he was devoured by Daggermouth,
the man-eating bluefish.

04:23.668 --> 04:26.046
You want to buy that boat?
Go ahead, take it.

04:26.173 --> 04:29.175
Don't expect me to fish your dead body
from an angry sea

04:29.300 --> 04:32.428
that gave you fair warning.

04:32.428 --> 04:36.057
Are you up for bids, too?
You are just precious.

04:38.059 --> 04:44.315
- Are you gonna miss me?
- Only until I go and buy a Hustler.

04:44.398 --> 04:47.652
I left you the number for the spa.
See you in a few days.

04:47.652 --> 04:50.782
Not if I strangle myself
with a seaweed wrap and die.

04:50.864 --> 04:53.370
You are dark!

04:56.495 --> 04:59.332
You haven't told me
how you expect to pay for that boat.

04:59.415 --> 05:02.669
There's got to be a hundred banks
that'll give me a loan.

05:04.753 --> 05:07.465
- So, you can really give me a loan?
- I sure can.

05:07.548 --> 05:11.218
What sets us apart from other banks
is that other banks are banks.

05:11.218 --> 05:16.432
- Now, I trust you have collateral.
- I got three kids.

05:16.517 --> 05:20.897
I'll take 'em. Just kidding.
Or maybe I'm not. Sign this.

05:21.022 --> 05:23.816
Here you go. Good luck!

05:26.528 --> 05:29.153
- What do you want on your thigh?
- I want a skull.

05:29.238 --> 05:32.994
OK. I can draw Kermit the Frog.
How about a nice Kermit the Frog?

05:33.117 --> 05:36.746
- No. I want a skull.
- OK. I'll go ahead and do Kermit the Frog.

05:38.748 --> 05:42.501
- Mom, this is so lame.
- Come on, Meg. Try to have fun.

05:42.584 --> 05:46.464
I promise after a few days you won't
remember the words "spring break".

05:46.464 --> 05:49.049
Hey, how about some TV?

05:49.174 --> 05:52.305
This is MTV
and we're rocking at spring break!

05:53.139 --> 05:56.475
Hey, this is VH1
and we're rocking at spring break.

05:56.475 --> 06:00.730
...leaving thousands injured.
For CNN, I'm Bernard Shaw,

06:00.855 --> 06:04.818
keeping it real and kicking ass
at spring break! Whoo!

06:06.570 --> 06:11.576
Here she is, boys. The S.S. More Powerful
than Superman, Batman, Spiderman

06:11.701 --> 06:13.869
and the Incredible Hulk Put Together.

06:13.993 --> 06:17.414
She's a fine vessel.
Welcome to the wharf. Name's Hennessey.

06:17.539 --> 06:20.335
Peter Griffin.
Friends call me Peter for short.

06:20.460 --> 06:26.090
I'll let you in on a secret, neighbour. The
best fishing is at latitude 42, longitude 71.

06:26.175 --> 06:28.383
- Keep that to yourself.
- Wow, thanks.

06:28.467 --> 06:31.388
I'll see you, fellas. I got some fish to catch.

06:34.516 --> 06:40.772
Let's see, latitude 42, longitude 71.
This is it. What the hell...?

06:41.522 --> 06:44.444
Papa, he killed Mordecai,
the Dancing Yiddish Clown!

06:44.444 --> 06:47.446
Stop crying.
You just became a man. Act like one.

06:48.196 --> 06:51.118
What's the big idea sending me
to that bar mitzvah?

06:51.118 --> 06:56.206
Cos I don't like you! We don't need any
more fishermen crowding up this wharf!

06:56.331 --> 06:59.958
- Fine. You want an enemy, you got one!
- Fine!

07:01.836 --> 07:04.048
There we are.

07:04.132 --> 07:06.758
Steve, you ever think
of growing a moustache?

07:11.554 --> 07:15.391
Nice fish you got there, Griffin.
What are you selling? Your bait?

07:15.515 --> 07:20.522
Nice face, Hennessey.
Yes! Me, one. You, zero.

07:20.605 --> 07:22.691
Hey!

07:24.986 --> 07:28.738
- Wow. So, how do you do it?
- Oh, you're very nice to ask.

07:28.863 --> 07:32.493
First, I hang the old worm out there.
They usually go for it.

07:32.618 --> 07:36.874
I jerk 'em around. They fight for a while.
Then they lay back and accept it.

07:37.000 --> 07:40.962
- How about we get together later?
- OK.

07:41.043 --> 07:43.549
What the hell...? Oh, dammit!

07:46.383 --> 07:49.511
Hey, what's going on here?

07:49.594 --> 07:52.432
Did you read the fine print
on this loan contract?

07:52.515 --> 07:57.228
If by read, you mean
imagined a naked lady, then yes.

07:57.311 --> 07:59.397
The bank's taking all our stuff.

07:59.522 --> 08:03.361
And if you don't pay them within 48 hours,
they get the house, too.

08:03.486 --> 08:06.696
Oh, boy! I get to go live at the bank!

08:10.785 --> 08:13.161
Did I ever tell you if you're on birth control

08:13.286 --> 08:17.334
and you take an antibiotic,
it makes it not work?

08:17.459 --> 08:22.672
Because no one told me.
I thought you should know.

08:22.756 --> 08:25.258
I don't really feel like talking right now.

08:25.383 --> 08:28.928
Fine. I just don't understand why we had
to leave the spa so early.

08:29.013 --> 08:33.933
I wanna go home and spend the next three
days in solitary confinement where I belong!

08:34.017 --> 08:36.104
Well, I tried.

08:50.202 --> 08:54.163
- What the hell are we doing here?
- This is where you wanted to be, right?

08:54.246 --> 08:56.248
Yeah. But not with you!

08:56.332 --> 08:58.834
Did you hear what happened
to that dude from UMass?

08:58.958 --> 09:02.923
He got so drunk he fell off
his hotel balcony! He's in a coma!

09:03.005 --> 09:06.676
- Oh, man! I want to party with him!
- You know it! Yeah!

09:06.676 --> 09:08.846
- Whoo! Whoo! Whoo!
- Yeah! Yeah!

09:09.596 --> 09:14.602
- Hey, look. Meg made it, you guys.
- Yeah. And she brought her mommy.

09:14.686 --> 09:18.355
- Oh, my God.
- Come on, Meg! Get out of the car!

09:18.437 --> 09:22.402
Like the kids say,
up your nose with a rubber hose!

09:22.527 --> 09:24.279
Whoo!

09:25.321 --> 09:28.158
Hey, look, everybody. It's Spuds MacKenzie!

09:28.242 --> 09:31.368
Aaargh!

09:32.412 --> 09:37.208
- Well, that's the last of the furniture.
- No TV. I miss my friends.

09:37.333 --> 09:40.546
John Ritter, Florence Henderson,
Alfonso Ribeiro.

09:40.672 --> 09:45.134
- Is he the guy from Silver Spoons?
- No. He was on French Prince of Bel-Air.

09:45.259 --> 09:48.596
- Fresh Prince.
- Fresh Prince of Bel-Air. I don't know if...

09:48.678 --> 09:50.139
- Hey, Alfonso.
- Yeah?

09:50.264 --> 09:52.225
- Were you on Silver Spoons?
- Yes.

09:52.348 --> 09:53.392
There you go.

09:55.478 --> 09:59.648
- Come on. Just a little higher, honey.
- Mom, I don't think I can...

09:59.733 --> 10:03.193
- Who's holding Lois?
- I don't know. Some dude named Mel.

10:03.193 --> 10:07.575
This is Carson Daly. We're live here
at spring break. Who wants to party?!

10:07.658 --> 10:11.746
OK, one, two, three, four, five...

10:11.746 --> 10:14.125
We'll need cake and juice for 14 people.

10:14.249 --> 10:18.626
Now let's go to Tom Green, who's
gonna do something really outrageous!

10:19.753 --> 10:23.508
Does anyone out there like me yet?
Can I stop this?

10:26.635 --> 10:28.722
What the hell are you doing in my house?

10:28.847 --> 10:32.392
Your house? This is my house.
My wife and I bought it from the bank.

10:32.476 --> 10:34.896
I still got another day to pay back the loan.

10:34.978 --> 10:38.104
The bank said you're a fat deadbeat loser.

10:38.229 --> 10:40.319
Fat deadbeat loser?

10:40.401 --> 10:45.322
While I may not agree with what you say,
I'll defend to the death your right to say it.

10:45.322 --> 10:48.950
There we are. It's a Van Gogh print.
Isn't it beautiful?

10:49.076 --> 10:52.705
I've fantasised about what this house
would be like with culture.

10:52.830 --> 10:54.375
- The port is good.
- Yes.

10:54.500 --> 10:55.416
- Indeed.
- Most certainly.

10:55.541 --> 10:56.458
- What year is it?
- '51.

10:56.583 --> 10:57.418
- Ahh.
- Delectable.

10:57.418 --> 10:58.335
- Indeed.
- Yes.

10:58.460 --> 10:58.961
- Oh, dear!
- What is it?

10:59.087 --> 11:00.838
- I've spontaneously combusted.
- I am sorry.

11:00.963 --> 11:02.508
I've grown tired of living.

11:02.632 --> 11:03.548
- Very good.
- For the best.

11:03.675 --> 11:05.761
- Yes, indeed.
- Is it raining again?

11:07.429 --> 11:10.767
Hey, did you hear the one about us?

11:11.474 --> 11:15.021
- Wow. You are such a good dancer.
- Way to go on that beer bong.

11:15.145 --> 11:17.522
- Yeah, no fake. No fake.
- Mom!

11:17.648 --> 11:21.277
- Hey! What are you doing here?
- What am I doing here?

11:21.401 --> 11:25.031
- I've been waiting out here for hours!
- What?

11:25.156 --> 11:28.993
You were gonna pop inside real quick
and find someone who looked like me

11:29.119 --> 11:32.330
so I could use their ID,
then you were supposed to come out

11:32.455 --> 11:35.875
and give me the ID so I can get inside!

11:36.834 --> 11:40.673
- What?
- God, it's like talking to a three-year-old!

11:40.798 --> 11:44.008
You need to learn how
to loosen up a little, toots.

11:44.134 --> 11:46.847
- You're loose enough for the both of us.
- What?

11:46.930 --> 11:51.726
- Nothing.
- That's right, nothing. Don't you sass me!

11:51.852 --> 11:55.187
Good evening. Stevenson residence.

11:55.272 --> 11:59.650
Chris, we've been over this a thousand times.
It's pronounced "Griffin".

11:59.776 --> 12:03.404
- Hi, Mom!
- Hi, Chris. Put your father on.

12:03.528 --> 12:09.036
- Hey, Dad?
- French guy says "Deodorant? What's that?"

12:10.828 --> 12:14.460
All right. All right.
I've got one. I've got one. OK.

12:14.585 --> 12:19.047
Two men are standing at the Pearly Gates.
Oh, God, wait. How did that one go?

12:19.172 --> 12:23.341
It turns out they're Siegfried and Roy.
I'm no good at telling jokes.

12:23.425 --> 12:27.805
- Dad, it's Mom.
- Oh, God. Please be Somerset Maugham.

12:27.931 --> 12:28.973
- Hello?
- Peter?

12:29.057 --> 12:32.519
- Damn!
- Calling to check in, see how you guys are.

12:32.602 --> 12:35.230
Oh, we're fine.

12:35.230 --> 12:37.942
- What's all that noise?
- Nothing. Nothing.

12:38.025 --> 12:42.404
- I need you to take out the trash.
- OK, Lois! Lois, I got to go.

12:42.527 --> 12:44.824
Holy crap, Brian! What am I gonna do?

12:44.909 --> 12:48.786
Lois will be home in a coupla days
and we're getting kicked out tomorrow.

12:48.869 --> 12:51.164
- What do you suggest?
- Get out your ring.

12:51.289 --> 12:53.248
- That's not gonna...
- Come on!

12:53.374 --> 12:55.460
Wonder Twin powers, activate!

12:55.543 --> 12:58.588
Form of... steam!

12:59.298 --> 13:01.508
We got these in a box of Frankenberry.

13:01.591 --> 13:06.721
A jackal! Jackal! It's a jackal! It looks
like a jackal! Jackal? It's a jackal! Jackal?

13:06.806 --> 13:09.223
- Time!
- It wasn't right the first time!

13:09.307 --> 13:14.228
Why the hell would it be right
the next ten times?! God!

13:17.858 --> 13:21.736
I am screwed. I'm gonna lose my house
and my boat and everything.

13:21.819 --> 13:24.116
How am I gonna come up with 50 grand?

13:24.242 --> 13:28.284
You could whore yourself out to
a thousand fat chicks for 50 bucks apiece.

13:28.410 --> 13:31.832
Or 50 really fat chicks
for a thousand bucks.

13:31.957 --> 13:37.046
What? Don't look at me like that. Fat chicks
need love, too. But they got to pay.

13:37.171 --> 13:39.256
Agh! What is this?

13:39.338 --> 13:43.094
Sea water, courtesy
of that gentleman over there.

13:43.219 --> 13:46.222
You need 50 grand, Griffin?
I got a suggestion for you.

13:46.347 --> 13:48.515
Why don't you kill Daggermouth?

13:50.394 --> 13:52.687
Maybe I will, Hennessey.

13:52.812 --> 13:56.568
You'd be buying yourself
a one-way ticket to a watery grave.

13:56.651 --> 14:01.570
Daggermouth is the meanest, most ruthless
creature that's ever inhabited the sea.

14:01.654 --> 14:04.910
Legend has it he dwells out
by Fish Stench Cove.

14:04.991 --> 14:08.746
He'll kill any man that comes near there.
I saw him once.

14:08.873 --> 14:13.458
Sure, I'm blind in one eye, and my other eye
was infected that day from picking at it,

14:13.542 --> 14:18.047
and I was tired, and I'd been swimming
in a pool with too much chlorine,

14:18.130 --> 14:21.675
and my glasses were at LensCrafters,
but I seen that fish!

14:21.800 --> 14:24.512
If there's 50 grand in it,
I don't think I got a choice.

14:24.512 --> 14:27.931
You can whore yourself out
to a thousand fat chicks for 50 bucks.

14:28.059 --> 14:30.644
- No, we covered that.
- You ain't got a chance.

14:30.771 --> 14:34.939
Daggermouth killed my friend Salty,
and he was twice the fisherman you are.

14:35.024 --> 14:37.651
And half the weight! Ooh...

14:37.651 --> 14:40.570
Hey, no! No! Hot!

14:40.652 --> 14:44.825
Lt'd be suicide to go after that fish.
There's got to be another way.

14:44.950 --> 14:48.163
- We could have a bake sale.
- I think that's a neat idea.

14:48.288 --> 14:51.416
No! I am not gonna let my family
live on the street.

14:51.416 --> 14:53.709
Not even if it means ending up like Shamus.

14:53.791 --> 14:57.671
Now, if you'll excuse me,
I have a date with destiny.

14:58.715 --> 15:02.677
- So were you, like, in an accident or what?
- No. Me father was a tree.

15:06.722 --> 15:08.811
What's wrong with me?

15:08.936 --> 15:13.188
I gotta be crazy to think I can kill that
man-eating fish. What the hell am I doing?

15:13.313 --> 15:16.734
Hey, hey, hey. Come on, Peter.
What kind of talk is that?

15:16.860 --> 15:20.404
Yeah, you can do it.
Who's my big brave boy, huh?

15:20.487 --> 15:22.908
- Me.
- Who's my big brave boy?

15:22.991 --> 15:26.120
Me.

15:30.289 --> 15:33.125
- This sucks, Mom.
- Meg, stop moping.

15:33.209 --> 15:37.381
These are the best years of your life.
Let's get up there and live a little.

15:40.299 --> 15:43.138
- I look like an idiot!
- No, you don't. Come on.

15:43.138 --> 15:46.348
Just move your hips a little like this.

15:46.473 --> 15:50.854
- Lois! Lois! Lois!
- Meg! Meg! Meg! Meg!

15:50.937 --> 15:55.524
Meg! Meg! Meg! Meg! Meg!

15:55.650 --> 15:58.569
Attagirl! Shake your moneymaker!

15:58.569 --> 16:02.617
Meg! Meg! Meg! Meg! Meg!
Meg! Meg! Meg! Meg!

16:02.743 --> 16:06.369
Oh, my God! It's a chick!

16:06.493 --> 16:10.665
- Ay, Dios mio, una chica!
- All right, everybody! This party's over!

16:10.748 --> 16:13.252
Why do you cops
always have to kill our buzz?

16:13.378 --> 16:16.590
He used a teenage colloquialism.
Get the tear gas.

16:20.052 --> 16:22.845
- Not so fast, big guy.
- What are you guys doing here?

16:22.970 --> 16:25.138
We're gonna help you kill the fish.

16:25.263 --> 16:29.937
- This will be dangerous. We could all die.
- Come on. You're our best friend.

16:30.062 --> 16:32.772
I can remember when you saved all our butts.

16:33.399 --> 16:34.733
Mnh-mnh. Mnh-mnh.

16:36.109 --> 16:37.234
Hyah!

16:37.361 --> 16:42.240
Too bad I didn't get there till after
the sodomy. Let's go kick some fish ass!

16:46.830 --> 16:49.874
I can't believe
I just showed everyone my tater tots.

16:49.874 --> 16:52.668
Worst of all,
now I'm gonna have a police record.

16:52.795 --> 16:54.963
If you're gonna grab ahold of life,

16:55.089 --> 16:58.216
you've gotta expect to get
your hands dirty once in a while.

16:58.299 --> 17:01.554
- It was cool that people noticed me.
- That's the spirit.

17:01.638 --> 17:04.264
OK, one, two, three... tuck and roll!

17:09.146 --> 17:11.855
We're right on course. Give me another beer.

17:11.980 --> 17:14.150
These are the precious moments.

17:14.275 --> 17:19.365
The four of us out at sea, miles away
from civilisation, tossing back brews.

17:19.490 --> 17:24.703
Amen to that. You guys, here's one for you.
Let's say none of us were married.

17:24.785 --> 17:27.206
If you could have any woman,
who would it be?

17:27.289 --> 17:29.083
- Mariel Hemingway.
- Really?

17:29.083 --> 17:31.460
- That's not a good choice.
- She's so jagged.

17:31.584 --> 17:35.004
I think she's very attractive
in a classical kind of way.

17:35.131 --> 17:37.215
But you could cut a roast on her face.

17:37.298 --> 17:42.012
- I would go with Margaret Thatcher.
- Why the hell Margaret Thatcher?

17:42.097 --> 17:45.016
Oh, so nobody here thinks power is sexy?

17:45.142 --> 17:48.477
- Not one of you finds power sexy?
- How about you, Peter?

17:48.561 --> 17:51.814
The chick with the three knockers
from Total Recall.

17:51.898 --> 17:55.152
- I never saw that movie.
- One of them was papier-mвchй.

17:55.236 --> 17:59.198
Can I change my answer...?
Of course I know it's paper! I don't care!

17:59.321 --> 18:02.324
What's wrong with you?
What about you, Quagmire?

18:02.450 --> 18:05.789
- Taylor Hanson.
- Taylor Hanson's a guy.

18:08.914 --> 18:14.337
You guys are yanking me.
"Let's put one over on old Quagmire. "

18:14.422 --> 18:17.340
No, he's actually a guy, Quagmire.

18:17.467 --> 18:21.430
Wha... Well, this is insane!
That's impossible!

18:22.263 --> 18:24.976
Oh, my God! Oh, my God!

18:25.060 --> 18:29.354
Oh, my God, I can't... Oh, God!
I got all these magazines!

18:29.436 --> 18:31.524
Oh, God! Oh, God!

18:34.234 --> 18:40.825
- This must be Fish Stench Cove.
- Now all we gotta do is find the fish.

18:40.908 --> 18:43.953
I wonder where that fish did go.

18:43.953 --> 18:47.498
A fish, a fish, a fishy-o!

18:57.719 --> 19:02.099
I heard that when Daggermouth eats you,
he devours your guts first.

19:02.099 --> 19:06.560
I heard he doesn't just eat you,
he eats your soul.

19:06.685 --> 19:11.357
I heard that one of Shannon Doherty's eyes
is off-centre cos it's trying to escape.

19:11.482 --> 19:14.193
Welcome, gentlemen.

19:14.276 --> 19:17.740
- Agh!
- It's him! Quick, shoot him!

19:17.824 --> 19:21.701
Not so fast! Perhaps I could
offer you a glass of port.

19:21.785 --> 19:25.122
And you, a glass of starboard.
That's a nautical joke.

19:25.248 --> 19:28.999
- I'm a fish. I'm also delightfully mad.
- Agh!

19:29.083 --> 19:31.503
Would you mind holding still for a moment?

19:31.586 --> 19:34.631
These antique pistols
take ten minutes to reload.

19:34.715 --> 19:38.260
- Peter, catch!
- Ow! Don't throw stuff at me, Joe!

19:38.387 --> 19:41.097
- Shoot him!
- Oh, yeah. Right.

19:45.766 --> 19:50.774
My God. Isn't it amazing that that's
what we all look like on the inside?

19:50.899 --> 19:53.819
- It's a robot, you idiot.
- Who are you?

19:53.819 --> 19:58.199
- I'm Salty.
- Everybody said you were killed by the fish.

19:58.199 --> 20:03.079
That's what I wanted. I disappeared
and spread the Daggermouth rumour myself.

20:03.204 --> 20:07.583
- Why?
- Merchandise. T-shirts, mugs, posters.

20:07.664 --> 20:10.586
I'm in talks with Nickelodeon
for a cartoon show.

20:10.711 --> 20:14.338
- I'd pair him with an effeminate cat.
- I'd watch that.

20:14.465 --> 20:16.634
- Me too.
- Sounds like a good balance.

20:16.762 --> 20:20.180
And now I'm gonna give you
$50,000 to be on your way.

20:20.305 --> 20:24.478
- $50,000? For what?
- To keep your mouth shut.

20:24.560 --> 20:27.268
The longer we stay here,
the more people will question

20:27.393 --> 20:29.898
how a fisherman
with no engineering background

20:29.981 --> 20:33.025
built a sophisticated talking fish robot.

20:34.986 --> 20:38.032
You know, honey,
I'm really sorry for how I acted.

20:38.032 --> 20:40.532
Getting drunk and ditching you at the bar,

20:40.617 --> 20:44.082
and letting those boys take pictures
of you sleeping.

20:44.082 --> 20:47.500
I was so busy having fun,
I guess I kind of ruined it for you.

20:47.625 --> 20:50.961
Uh-oh. We got company.

20:54.507 --> 20:58.554
- Looks like your friends are back, Mom.
- Meg! Meg! Meg! Meg!

20:58.679 --> 21:02.101
No, I think this one's all yours.

21:02.226 --> 21:05.851
- Whoo! Yeah! You go, girl!
- One's an innie and one's an outie.

21:08.565 --> 21:12.442
And now, back to "Daggermouth
and Boom Boom" on Nickelodeon.

21:12.527 --> 21:15.030
Boom Boom, did you do
your exercises today?

21:15.155 --> 21:19.325
Yes. I did 20 laps.
And I'm about to do 20 more.

21:19.409 --> 21:21.913
- Oh, you!
- Yipes!

21:24.956 --> 21:28.294
Peter, I'm so glad being a fisherman
is working out for you.

21:28.378 --> 21:32.130
I got to admit I half expected to come home,
and our stuff would be gone,

21:32.256 --> 21:34.341
and we'd owe somebody a lot of money.

21:34.425 --> 21:38.386
- How can you half expect something?
- It's just a turn of phrase.

21:38.512 --> 21:42.892
- How do you turn a phrase?
- God, you're dumb. Thank God for that ass.

21:42.976 --> 21:45.395
Now, come here and kiss me.

21:45.479 --> 21:47.690
- Good night, honey.
- Good night, Lois.

21:47.773 --> 21:50.275
- Good night, Jim and Abby.
- Good night.

21:50.400 --> 21:55.698
Not now, Abby.

21:55.699 --> 22:56.699
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru